The approach:

Yomonsni borrows ideas and concepts liberally from many diverse arenas of thought, diet, exercise, philosophy, science, culture, and growth. Not satisfied with approaches that work on part of the mind/body/self without taking the whole into consideration, the approach is to work on all aspects of the mind/body/self within an integrated growth path. Yomonsni works with gradual changes and growth. 

Body - is the base physicality of existence. This is your physical form, your fitness, your health, your hygiene, body language, voice. 

Mind - is the sum of thought, knowledge, processing. This ties to the physical because your mind is a physical thing that exists in your neurobiology - your memories and knowledge have physical basis encoded in neural connections, your perceptions of the world are processed in this physicality. 

Self - is the core of connection, creativity. This is the 'you' that thinks, your inner voice, your creativity, passion, presences and connection. 


Who we are is all three layers. Our self is our identity, filters through our mind - our knowledge and experiences, and then expresses through our body - the physicality of our existance.

Imagine you are wearing formal wear, the way that you interact with others changes from the way you interact with the same people if you are instead wearing simple work attire, and it changes again if you are wearing exercise clothing. There is a noticible impact on our psychology depending upon the clothes we wear - they act as a filter to our identity. So, to remove all filters, and work with a radically complete openness within the practice, all work is conducted without clothing. 

